| hakanensari | 63 | 22.8% | 1 | 2014-04-15 | inactive |
| Gonzalo Rodriguez | 50 | 18.1% | 24 | 2026-03-09 | active |
| Divya Rao | 40 | 14.5% | 1 | 2026-01-28 | active |
| Hye-jin Park | 27 | 9.8% | 2 | 2026-02-20 | active |
| Brad Lindsay | 19 | 6.9% | 1 | 2018-02-06 | inactive |

18 more authors hold the rest.

- **Ask Gonzalo Rodriguez first.** Gonzalo has the most lines of anyone still active, and the most commits here (24, from 2018-01-25 to 2026-03-09). Gonzalo also holds the most lines in the whole repo, 46.1% of 4,138 lines.
- **Review: Gonzalo Rodriguez and Divya Rao.** Both are active.
- **Hye-jin Park is a third reviewer option.** Hye-jin is active and holds 27 lines.
- **hakanensari** wrote the first version, 63 lines in a single commit in 2014. By the tool's line ranking, hakanensari is the top owner and in its top-three suggestion. hakanensari has been inactive since 2014-04-15, so I wouldn't count on a review from them. Brad Lindsay is also inactive.

**Caveats**
- **Bus factor:** 3, meaning the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted. Here that is hakanensari, Gonzalo Rodriguez and Divya Rao, together 55.4% of 276 lines. To reach 80% takes 7 authors. Both figures are for `store_proxy` only. For the whole repo, the bus factor is 2 and it takes 7 authors to reach 80%.
- **Line counts and recent changes:** 33 of 290 lines (11.4%) were moved or copied here from other paths, so they are credited to whoever wrote them. This includes `dalli_proxy.rb` and `redis_store_proxy.rb`. Recent commits such as "Extract Dalli read/write/increment/delete into DalliAccessors" and "Add ttl to RedisCacheStoreProxy" are not necessarily reflected in these totals.
- **Identity merges:** Gonzalo Rodriguez also appears as "Gonzalo" under the same address, and I counted them as one. That adds 50 lines to the 50 shown, because the table already uses the merged name. Jonathan del Strother appears under two addresses (13 and 3 lines), which I merged in memory as a guess from names and addresses. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`.
- **Copy detection:** The figures use `-w -M -C`. Without copy detection, hakanensari has 46 lines (16.7%) and Gonzalo Rodriguez has 43 (15.6%). Mei Tanaka has 10 lines (3.6%) with it and 38 (13.8%) without. Gonzalo Rodriguez and Divya Rao still rank in the top three either way. The ranking could shift for hakanensari, who stays first only with copy detection.
- **Excluded:** The bot `github-actions[bot]` is excluded (14 lines, 1 commit) and gets no credit. No reformat commits were set aside.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked and set aside 0 commits. One more looks mechanical and I kept it: `20d6682` "style: fix Lint/HandleExceptions rubocop" by Gonzalo Rodriguez, 2 surviving lines. It does not change the ranking.

These numbers measure whose code is still here. They don't show who understands the design, or who reviewed it. Ask Gonzalo Rodriguez in case that history isn't visible in the lines.
